The window model kdos-comp carries out, as a table of rectangles.

This is the contract libkwm is written against. Every row here was derived by
reading named compositor or libkwm source, never by taste. Where libkwm and a
row disagree, the row is right and the library is wrong.

Six sections, one per decision:

  tile   the tiled-state transition   src/view.c view_snap_to_edge(), libkwm kwm_tile_next()
  geom   a tiled state becomes a rect src/view.c view_get_edge_snap_box(), libkwm kwm_tile_geom()
  place  where a new window lands     src/placement.c placement_find_best(), libkwm kwm_place()
  edge   the neighbour-edge search    src/edges.c, src/snap.c check_edge(); rows clip, best, btwn
  wsadj  the nearest occupied workspace src/workspaces.c get_adjacent_occupied()
  drag   when a press becomes a drag  libkwm kwm_drag_threshold()

Each section header in geometry.txt names its functions; a compositor path
(src/..., include/...) is relative to src/desktop/kdos-comp. Read geometry.txt with it. A row that cannot
be traced to one of those functions does not belong in the file.
